## Existing historical Stage and lossless representation

All current Stage records stay selected, including failed2eb/d632,300e,2f3,b327,23f7,4828,579 and both diagnostic histories. Keep primary reports/source excerpts/commands/exits/readbacks directly readable. Canonical deterministic gzip companions replace large selected plaintext only after separate root admission of relocation/removal and exact verification; originals remain in their current location during compression/review. In particular do not silently delete the full-module historical audits merely because current proof passes.

Concrete canonical threshold: every existing nongzip regular file over1MiB (244files/5,069,471,729bytes), plus each newly selected LL/S/source archive over1MiB, is eligible for `gzip -n -1 -k`. Retain small files and already compressed gzip/wheel unchanged. Use one canonical companion per original byte identity; existing verified same-content companions may be reused only after full readback. Deterministic same-byte gzip blobs naturally deduplicate in Git even when historical paths differ. No tar containing all full targets and no second redundant large plaintext copy is proposed.

For each actual selection write a path map with original absolute/Stage-relative path, archive-relative companion path, original size/mode/SHA256, stored size/SHA256 and compression status. Keep every original absolute-path manifest verbatim. Reconstruction: restore named originals with `gzip -dc ARCHIVED.gz > ORIGINAL`; verify full manifest before interpreting receipts or replaying commands. Preserve basename/path roles using the map, not flattened ambiguous hashes. Replay depends on matching Rust SDK/production registry lock/interpreter/tool identities and recorded profiles; copied artifacts allow read-only body proof without a compiler run.

