For every newly compressed path require actual gzip exit0, `gzip -t`0, full `cmp ORIGINAL <(gzip -dc ORIGINAL.gz)`0 and decompressed SHA equal original's retained manifest. Verify each copied noncompressed artifact against its original manifest, all selected emitted counterparts nonempty and no symlink-to-disposable-target substitution. Record actual stored size: any oversized gzip is a real unresolved publication blocker, not presumed compressible. Original relocation/removal is a distinct root-admitted phase after qualified lossless companions/readbacks, retaining owned originals outside the selected publication directory until remote archive verification/cleanup authorization.

## Size estimate and actual capture constraints

No new compression has run, so no exact final compressed size exists. Actual existing15gzip files total387,772,112bytes. Three measured large LLVM examples have original172,422,504/187,097,013/187,178,194 and stored34,467,226/37,360,385/37,375,159bytes (about20%). Applying that observed ratio to the244eligible originals gives about1.014GB; existing noneligible/current gzip+small records contribute about0.711GB, so existing Stage would be roughly1.73GB of stored file bytes. A15–30% ratio range yields about1.47–2.23GB. These are estimates, not publication admission. After separate compression admission, group actual originals by canonical SHA/size, verify byte equality before deduplication, compress one representative per identity and map every historical role/path to reconstructible stored bytes. Measure actual stored unique-byte sum, largest blob and actual capture pack before publication. Preserve every historical record and original until authorized archival/readback/cleanup. GitHub's single-push limit is2GiB, so the20% estimate cannot establish fit; do not use LFS, another repository or multi-push bypass to evade that guard.

Inspected actual ghprsq/capture implementation has **no100MB filtering rule**: it captures every selected file, ignores ignore/attribute/filter exclusions, scans stable snapshots, validates the tree, and merely prints an all-evidence notice above20,000,000bytes. The external forge blocks files over100MiB (104,857,600bytes); use conservative100,000,000stored-byte preflight ceiling. [GitHub's actual file-limit documentation](https://docs.github.com/en/repositories/working-with-files/managing-large-files/about-large-files-on-github). Current nine>100MB/eight>100MiB files therefore require packaging, not silent capture exclusion.

